# 20. Final Project Objective

The objective is to transform the existing Stock Change module from a manually operated product-selection process into an automated product identification and stock processing workflow.

A user should be able to place 30 different products in front of a camera, capture one photograph, and let the system independently process each product.

The system should:

- Detect every visible product it can reliably distinguish.
- Read available barcodes.
- Identify products without barcodes through image matching.
- Search external product information sources.
- Retrieve product specifications.
- Determine package sizes and units per package where verifiable.
- Compare products against registered business records.
- Check stock operations in progress.
- Identify existing and new products.
- Display all results for confirmation.
- Transfer confirmed products into Stock Change.

**The most important requirement is that the system must perform actual searching and identification, not simply display information from a predefined list.**

It must use the business database first where possible, then external product sources when necessary, and clearly distinguish verified information from uncertain matches.

The existing Stock Management System must remain intact. This is an additional capability integrated into its existing workflow, not a replacement for the current stock management functionality.